@startuml repos-and-release
' How a machine's integration repo, its service repos, the package repos and the images work together, and how they
' end up in a release. The model of PLAN.md step 4 (imports and a lock), with the example names of the starters.
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #555555
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #888888
}

title Repos, images and a machine's release

package "GitHub (private, over SSH)" as gh {
  rectangle "**Integration repo**, one per machine\n----\ndependencies.repos: the machine's services\nflexcompose.yaml: imports [example_app, example_driver]\nflexcompose.release.yaml: each service builds from the locked tree\nlock.repos: exact commit of every repo (lock.sh writes it)\nlock.sh, release.sh, bundle/, .devcontainer/<service>/" as integ #E8F0FE

  rectangle "**Service repo** example_app\n(runs from source in a dev box)\n----\npackages\ndependencies.repos\nDockerfile: stages resolve, workspace, build, release\nflexcompose.yaml (workspace: true)\nflexcompose.release.yaml: image, build, command\nbootstrap.sh, .devcontainer/" as app #E6F4EA

  rectangle "**Service repo** example_driver\n(runs as its image, also in a dev box)\n----\npackages\ndependencies.repos\nDockerfile\nflexcompose.yaml (build:, no workspace)\nflexcompose.release.yaml" as drv #E6F4EA

  rectangle "**Package repos**\n(shared between services and machines)\n----\npackages\ndependencies.repos: what they use in turn" as pkgs #FEF7E0
}

database "Registry cboost-c-nas:5100" as reg {
  rectangle "**Base image**\ncboost-ros2-jazzy:0.3.0\n(ROS 2, cdr, vcs)" as base #F3E8FD
}

package "Developer PC: ./release.sh on the commit tagged v1.1.0" as pc {
  rectangle "**Locked tree** (temporary folder)\nvcs import lock.repos, .git removed\nexample_app/, example_driver/, package repos\n+ the integration repo's two templates" as tree
  rectangle "**flexcompose generate**, in the locked tree\nimports each service's flexcompose.yaml,\nits flexcompose.release.yaml, then the machine's\n→ compose.release-build.yaml, compose.release.yaml" as fc
  rectangle "**docker compose build**, per service\nits own Dockerfile, BASE_IMAGE = base image\ncontext workspace = the locked tree\n(replaces the stages resolve and workspace)\nstage build: colcon → /opt/app\nstage release: base image + /opt/app" as build
  rectangle "**Release images**\nexample-app:1.1.0\nexample-driver:1.1.0\n(compiled packages only, no C/C++/Rust source)" as imgs #F3E8FD
  rectangle "**release-v1.1.0/**\nimages.tar, compose.release.yaml, .env\nlock.repos, start.sh, stop.sh, update.sh\nSHA256SUMS" as bundle #FCE8E6

  tree --> fc
  fc --> build
  build --> imgs
  imgs --> bundle : docker save
}

package "Machine (offline)" as machine {
  rectangle "releases/\nrelease-v1.0.0/, release-v1.1.0/\ncurrent → release-v1.1.0" as rels
  rectangle "**Docker**\ndocker load, up -d, never pulls\nkeeps the images of the newest 3" as eng
  rels --> eng : update.sh
}

' How the repos refer to each other.
integ --> app : dependencies.repos lists it;\nflexcompose.yaml imports it
integ --> drv : dependencies.repos lists it;\nflexcompose.yaml imports it
app --> pkgs : dependencies.repos
drv --> pkgs : dependencies.repos
pkgs --> pkgs : dependencies.repos

' What a release is made of.
integ ..> tree : lock.repos: every repo\nat its locked commit
app ..> tree
drv ..> tree
pkgs ..> tree
base ..> build : FROM
bundle --> rels : copy (USB, file share)

note right of integ
  ./lock.sh resolves dependencies.repos with cdr,
  through every service's and package's own
  dependencies.repos, in a fresh folder.
  Only this file settles a conflict between pins.
  Review the diff, commit lock.repos, tag v1.1.0.
end note

note bottom of app
  Alone: its own dev box (src/ = this repo,
  deps/ = its dependencies) and
  docker build --ssh default -t <name> .
  In the machine's dev box: the same box,
  as one container among the services.
end note

@enduml
